{"repositoryId":883025851,"availability":"available","full":"mizdra/css-modules-kit","name":"css-modules-kit","description":"A toolkit for making CSS Modules useful.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":203,"forks":15,"created":"2024-11-04T08:50:02Z","updated":"2026-10-08T13:05:11Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["css-modules","typescript-language-server-plugin"],"demo":"https://stackblitz.com/~/github.com/mizdra/css-modules-kit-example","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:24.162Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:24.162Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:24.162Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T16:01:24.162Z","stars":203,"forks":15}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["By default, CSS Modules have limited language features in editors. For example:","It has been difficult to solve these issues because the TypeScript Language Server (tsserver) does not load CSS files. TSServer does not know which part of the code to \"Go to Definition\" for, nor which part of the code to rename.","CSS Modules Kit solves this problem by using the TypeScript Language Service Plugin and Volar.js. They extend tsserver to load .module.css files. As a result, rich language features become available. Moreover, it works with various editors."],"features":["Clicking on styles.button does not \"Go to Definition\" in Button.module.css.","Renaming styles.button modifies the code in Button.tsx but not in Button.module.css.","Performing \"Find All References\" for styles.button finds references in Button.tsx, not in Button.module.css."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mizdra/css-modules-kit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2f39baff4a6748b5a16a1832563a5443d18653d32745b77d7715b83cfd96d54c","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:24.266Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:24.266Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"By default, CSS Modules have limited language features in e